sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the 10.32 nm Chlamydomonas eyespot pigment stripe (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 77.6/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Reference parameters a=0.07, b=0.95, Du=1, Dv=36 (not slot 195's 1.63/0.43/14/10/140). The spatial unit sets lambda(k_max)=10.32 nm. Onset lambda(k_c)=6.99 nm. Linear-regime finite differences track the analytical fastest mode at Pearson r=0.9997, RMSE=0.20 nm, across Dv in {18,24,32,36,44,58,76}. Age 0 Ma. Unfiltered SEM cell median was 1.29 um and is not accepted in this pass. Overall 77.6/100 (faithfulness 74.4, reproducibility 84.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 70, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 68, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/chlamydomonas_reinhardtii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 530265 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 79b760e1b14cd10d4b6c6c87a239cc85a30b9290dd19deab4135c79cdc7c36fd (sha256 79b760e1b14cd10d4b6c6c87a239cc85a30b9290dd19deab4135c79cdc7c36fd), spec_fingerprint c41079d08516e24418edacb13a3820b8f31bff46de38d0a93c0cb0ebc5f205ac. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c41079d08516e24418edacb13a3820b8f31bff46de38d0a93c0cb0ebc5f205ac; artifact_sha256: 79b760e1b14cd10d4b6c6c87a239cc85a30b9290dd19deab4135c79cdc7c36fd; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/chlamydomonas_reinhardtii_turing_wavelength_s0/chlamydomonas_reinhardtii_specimen.jpg=7f2a2df501eb7977...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a homogeneous steady state can be unstable to a finite critical wavenumber k_c. | Schnakenberg 1979: activator-inhibitor kinetics du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v. | Dieckmann 2003 and Kreimer 2008: the Chlamydomonas eyespot is stacked carotenoid granules under the plasma membrane. | Foster and Smyth 1980: the eyespot stack acts as a quarter-wave light antenna. | Boyd et al. 2011: EYE2 and EYE3 are required for eyespot assembly. | Kato et al. 2012: channelrhodopsin is the light-gated channel associated with the eyespot.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian, onset k_c, and argmax of the linear growth rate sigma(k) for the Schnakenberg system. | Spatial calibration so the reference fastest wavelength is 10.32 nm = 1.032e-8 m (log10 = -7.986). | Explicit finite-difference check of that wavelength on a periodic six-stripe patch (61.92 nm).; transfer_boundary: A continuum reaction-diffusion description at 10 nm is a reduced model of pigment aggregation, not a measured morphogen pair. | The chronoseries is 1/1 (Holocene only). The 3.2 nm monomer and the ~93 nm quarter-wave spacing are scale neighbors, not fossil chronospecies.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that 10.32 nm was read off an electron micrograph as a published lattice constant. | Does not claim to replace the EYE2/EYE3 assembly pathway. | Does not claim the SEM resolves the 10 nm stripe. The GIF keeps the real cell silhouettes and modulates their interior.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1: Restrict SEM diameters to isolated cell bodies between 3 and 12 um so debris and the merged cluster do not set the median (Pass 1 unfiltered median was 1.29 um).",
            "remediation needed: R2: Record orientation, radial-FFT, and coherency similarities separately, and keep the negative-control and autocatalysis-ablation sigmas in the scored measurements.",
            "remediation needed: R3: Credit the saturated-versus-linear wavelength as a second parameter regime, not only the linear Dv sweep." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.776"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second provider in this cloud loop)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
}

